    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Kyle Tucker**, whose 77.36 efficiency score marks him as our premier play. Facing a favorable matchup against Marte (xERA 5.16), **Kyle Tucker** maximizes his utility with a massive +19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile. Close behind in the pecking order is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, projected at a 73.66. Even with his lineup spot currently pending, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a significant +14% platoon edge against Pfaadt, and he remains a primary weapon for our Roto objectives. Meanwhile, the combination of **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and **Gunnar Henderson** (64.70) remains essential; both receive a tactical bump from Gasser\u2019s slow delivery, which creates opportunistic conditions for stolen base attempts\u2014a critical variable given our focus on the scarce SB category.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 51.90 score. Despite a strong +19% SP skill boost against Lopez, the optimizer favored the higher baseline production and order security offered by the starters. **Miguel Vargas** also lurked on the bubble with a 50.63, but his recent output and platoon disadvantages against Jobe rendered him a secondary option today. We remain cautious regarding **Liam Hicks** and **Josh Jung**, who hold the lowest scores in our active lineup at 47.21 and 53.16 respectively. While **Liam Hicks** carries a modest platoon edge, his floor is thin; we are monitoring the lineup status for **Heliot Ramos** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** closely, as any shift from their assumed batting order could force a re-evaluation of our efficiency targets. As for **Luis Robert Jr.**, he remains sidelined on the IL, leaving the heavy lifting to our core of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Drake Baldwin**.",
